// H9a acceptance area (d) — a params theta forcing a real binder pass.
// Two `params:` fields (one defaulted) route to the binder (NOT a bypass), so a
// genuine binder pass over the declared params runs before the body. DECISION
// (production conformance): the binder runs OFF-session and INVISIBLE — its
// three-arm envelope JSON is NEVER streamed to the user / stdout. On a
// successful bind the observable proof is the `bind_echo` success note
// (`Running /acc-params-binder: …`). The `bind_model:` is provider-qualified
// because a bare id can be ambiguous across configured providers, and it names
// the model the shared live-suite preference rule resolves first: this is the
// only committed fixture file the acceptance half drives to a real binder
// call, so pinning it to a model the rule would never pick hides every
// request-shape fact that holds only on the preferred model (bug 0064). The
// area-(d) driver rewrites this
// line from `resolveAcceptanceHost()` before every spawn, so the committed
// value cannot drift away from the rule. A non-bypass theta with no resolvable
// binder model fails to load. The body is a pure-literal `respond`.
"ok"
